# Gitignored files a fresh worktree needs. Syntax is .gitignore's; a file is copied only when it
# matches a pattern here and is gitignored, so tracked files are never duplicated. Claude Code applies
# this to every worktree it creates. Neither .ai/agentic.config.local.json nor
# .claude/settings.local.json: a worktree reads both from its main checkout, and a copy of the
# config layer would go stale and win over it.
# The hook dispatcher runs from the worktree's own node_modules, so a commit before `pnpm install`
# fails instead of skipping the hook.
.vite-hooks/_/
